@ilyavolodin @ljharb how about something like this:

``` javascript
const npmOutput = shell.exec(`npm info ${packageName} peerDependencies --json`, {silent: "true"}).stdout;
const peerDependencies = JSON.parse(npmOutput);
```

Would it be safe to assume that an npm executable is present? Otherwise we could still fall back to a hardcoded version..

(I was actually hacking a bit on this the other day, but paused it for now to pursue some JSCS milestone issues)
